user:
Generate an adjuster memo narrative comparing these two estimates.

Primary Estimate: {primary_name}
Comparison Estimate: {comparison_name}

Analysis Results:
Overall Direction: {overall_delta_direction}
Confidence: {confidence}

Category Analyses:
{category_analyses_json}

Scope Gaps Identified:
{scope_gaps_json}

Respond with JSON matching this exact structure:
{{
  "overview": "2-3 sentences explaining the delta",
  "key_drivers": [
    {{
      "category": "category name",
      "amounts": "$X vs $Y (delta $Z)",
      "narrative": "Two sentences explaining what specific items drive this delta"
    }}
  ],
  "scope_observations": ["Specific scope item missing or different"],
  "suggested_followups": ["Request itemized breakdown of X"]
}}

CRITICAL RULES:
- overview sentence 1: State delta amount between {primary_name} and {comparison_name}
- overview sentence 2: NAME THE TOP 2-3 TRADE CATEGORIES driving the variance with percentages
- overview sentence 3: Explain the PATTERN (replacement vs repair, full scope vs limited, etc.)
- NEVER use vague phrases like "scope of work", "extensive replacements", "limited repairs"
- ALWAYS name SPECIFIC items: "impact windows", "architectural shingles", "panel upgrade"
- narrative: Two sentences naming WHAT ITEMS are included/excluded, not just that a delta exists
- amounts: Format as "{primary_name}: $X. {comparison_name}: $Y. Delta: $Z"
- scope_observations: Name specific line items, not categories
- suggested_followups: Actionable items for resolution
